				"bounds": {
					"height": 30,
					"width": 195,
					"x": -289.92987060546875,
					"y": 616.633544921875
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-1296-4264-A646-5CE3BE529286",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffae7bff",
				"constants": {
					"input0": {
						"type": "float2",
						"value": [
							0,
							0
						]
					}
				},
				"hidden": [
					"flow",
					"input0-type",
					"input0-dimensions"
				],
				"name": "Negate"
			},
			"100": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "TRANSPARENCY\n\nWe start by creating an option to add transparency to the clip.\nThe Threshold node is a nice way to create a mask with a LoFi quality to it\n\nTo LoFi it even further you could add a Resize node, resizing the texture to 1\/2 , 1\/4 or 1\/8th of the patch."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 475.57427978515625,
					"width": 990.3121337890625,
					"x": 262.28173828125,
					"y": -426.1800537109375
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffff6a00",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"101": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "MIXING\n\nThe recolored textures get sent to Layer 2 (on top of Layer 1).\nLayer 1 receives the original clip and has a toggle to turn it on and off."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 522.09228515625,
					"width": 676.59130859375,
					"x": 2237.40869140625,
					"y": -367.094970703125
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "fff26eb5",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"102": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "COLOR MODES\n\nDon't be scared of this huge mess, it is very simple and repetitive.\nWe recolor the clips using the AddSubtract node.\nThat node wants a float 3 so it can adjust the red, green and blue channels respectively.\n\nWhat we do in this bit is simply creating a whole bunch of Float 3 values that we can send into the AddSubtract node.\nWe start with a single Float In node renamed to \"Color Intensity\".\nThis value gets packed into all different kinds of combinations like single value, double value, negated value , double negated and so on.\nYou can easily make your own channel combos if you like.\n\nGroups of 6 float 3 values get joined in the Join node and sent to the Switch node.\nWe create 4 groups of 6, giving us 4 distinct visuals styles for the user to switch between using the Choice In node renamed \"Color Mode\""
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 3188.52490234375,
					"width": 1803.9002685546875,
					"x": -484.655517578125,
					"y": 1019.865478515625
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffe53357",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"103": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "COLOR SHIFTING\n\nThe Add Subtract node takes our 6 textures and applies the color mode to it that we've generated below. After that the instanced textures become a single texture again using the Merge node, to save on processing power(removing the need for an instanced Video Mixer)."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 295.476898193359375,
					"width": 763.51971435546875,
					"x": 1433.1473388671875,
					"y": 454.775665283203125
				},
				"class": {
