					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "RANDOMIZING POSITION\n\nWe want to shift the copies of the original clip around, but we want to keep the resolution of the composition in mind.\nThis is why we start with the Patch Info node, which gives us the resolution, which we divide by 4 to introduce some boundaries.\nThis value gets multiplied with the Float In node named \"Distance\".\nThe result is that we have a user-defined distance slider, whose values are based on the resolution.\nWe use OnChange to convert from signal to event flow and use these distance values for the random node (set to 6 instances).\n\n\nThe Random node can be either triggered manually with the Manual Shift Trigger In or by a metronome.\nWe give the user the option to smooth the output of the Random node to add even more flexibility to their fingertips before using the values in the Transform node to move the images around."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 903.4814453125,
					"width": 2046.2645263671875,
					"x": -797.7203369140625,
					"y": 76.07834625244140625
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffae7bff",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"106": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "SILKSCREENSHIFT\n\nSilkScreenShift demonstrates how copying and changing the incoming texture multiple times can lead to some interesting effects.\n\nThis effect takes the original texture, copies it 6 times and recolorizes each copy differently. \nThe concept behind this effect came from silk screen printing, where you can have 1 screen and print it multiple times each time with different colors.\n\nEven though this patch includes some big parts, most of it is repetitive, so once you get one bit, you get 'em all! Now go get 'em tiger!"
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 252.3663787841796875,
					"width": 675.833740234375,
					"x": -452.6314697265625,
					"y": -426.097442626953125
				},
